{"G1188":{"id":"G1188","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1188","disambiguated_id":"G1188 =","unique_id":"G1188","headword":"δεξιός","transliteration":"dexios","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"right","definition_en":"δεξιός, -ά, -όν \n [in LXX chiefly for יָמִין ;] \nthe right: Mat.5:29, Jhn.18:10, al.; ὅπλα δ., weapons carried in the right hand, i.e. for offence, 2Co.6:7 ; ἡ δ. χείρ, Mat.5:30, Luk.6:6, al.; ἡ δ. (sc. χείρ), Mat.6:3, al.; ἐπὶ τὴν δ., in the right hand (R, txt., on R, mg.), Rev.5:1; διδόναι τὴν δ., in friend­ship (Deiss., BS, 251), Gal.2:9; metaphorically of power, τῇ δ. αὐτοῦ, Act.2:33 5:31; τὰ δ., the right side, Mrk.16:5; ἐκ δεξιῶν, on the right hand, with genitive, Mat.25:33, 34, Mrk.15:27, Luk.1:11, al.; of a place of honour in the Messianic Kingdom (cf. 3Ki.2:19, Psa.44(45):10), καθίσαι ἐκ δεξιῶν, Mat.20:21, Mrk.10:37; of the heavenly session of Christ, Mat.26:64, Mrk.14:62, Heb.1:13 (Cremer, 172) \n (AS)","source_line":1320}],"occurrence_count":54,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"direita","count":50},{"gloss":"direito","count":3},{"gloss":"colunas","count":1}]},"G1424":{"id":"G1424","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1424","disambiguated_id":"G1424 =","unique_id":"G1424","headword":"δυσμή","transliteration":"dusmē","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"west","definition_en":"δυσμή, -ῆς, ἡ\n (= δύσις, δύνω), [in LXX for בּוֹא, עֲרָבָה, etc. ;] \nmostly in pl., opposite to ἀνατολαί; \n __1. a setting, as of the sun (accusative to Thayer, see word, so perhaps in Luk.12:54). \n __2. the quarter of sunset, the west: anarth., Mat.8:11 24:27, Luk.12:54 13:29, Rev.21:13.†\n (AS)","source_line":1556}],"occurrence_count":5,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"ocidente","count":5}]},"G1782":{"id":"G1782","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1782","disambiguated_id":"G1782 =","unique_id":"G1782","headword":"ἐντεῦθεν, ἔνθεν","transliteration":"enteuthen, enthen","lexical_morphology":"G:ADV","gloss_en":"from here","definition_en":"ἐντεῦθεν \n adv. (ἔνθεν), [in LXX chiefly for זֶה ;] \n__1. of place, hence: Luk.4:9 13:31, Jhn.2:16 7:3 14:31 18:36; ἐ. καὶ ἐ. (for cl. ἔνθεν κ. ἔνθεν), on this side and on that, on each side, Jhn.19:18; similarly, ἐ. καὶ ἐκεῖθεν, Rev.22:2. \n __2. Of time, thereupon. \n __3. Causal; hence, therefore: Jas.4:1.†\n ἔνθεν, \n adv., [in LXX for זֶה, פֹּה, etc. ;] \nhence: Mat.17:20, Luk.16:26.†\n (AS)","source_line":1923}],"occurrence_count":10,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"daqui","count":6},{"gloss":"lado","count":2},{"gloss":"cada","count":1},{"gloss":"acaso","count":1}]},"G203":{"id":"G203","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0203","disambiguated_id":"G0203 =","unique_id":"G0203","headword":"ἀκροβυστία","transliteration":"akrobustia","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"uncircumcision","definition_en":"ἀκροβυστία, -ας, ή\n (perh. an Alexandrian form of cl. ἀκροποσθία; cf. MM, VGT, see word) [in LXX for עׇרְלָה ;] \nthe prepuce, foreskin (LXX), hence abstr., uncircumcision: Act.11:3, Rom.2:25-27 3:30 4:10-12, 1Co.7:18-19, Gal.5:6 6:15, Col.2:13 3:11 By meton., the uncircumcised: Rom.4:9, Gal.2:7, Eph.2:11.†\n (AS)","source_line":302}],"occurrence_count":20,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"incircuncisão","count":8},{"gloss":"incircunciso","count":5},{"gloss":"incircuncisos","count":4},{"gloss":"circuncidados","count":2},{"gloss":"circuncidado","count":1}]},"G22":{"id":"G22","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0022","disambiguated_id":"G0022 =","unique_id":"G0022","headword":"ἄγαμος","transliteration":"agamos","lexical_morphology":"G:N-M/F","gloss_en":"unmarried","definition_en":"ἄ-γαμος, -ον \n [in LXX: 4Ma.16:9 * ;] \nunmarried: 1Co.7:8, 32; fem. (= cl. ἄνανδρος), ib. 11, 34.†\n (AS)","source_line":114}],"occurrence_count":4,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"solteiros","count":1},{"gloss":"casar","count":1},{"gloss":"solteiro","count":1},{"gloss":"solteira","count":1}]},"G2265":{"id":"G2265","source":"TBESG